A CUDA warp is a group of 32 GPU threads that execute instructions together. Threads in a warp can work on different data, but if they take different branches, the GPU executes the different paths with only the relevant threads active, which can reduce efficiency. For good performance, minimize branch divergence and have neighboring threads access neighboring memory locations.

